<!--
    An even ARM function symbol starts A32 code (`option armfuncmode on|off`,
    default on, GH-842).

    The XML wrapper only provides the harness architecture. Every pass clears
    it and loads one of the synthetic ARM32 ELFs from
    `arm_funcmode_le32.py`: an A32 `entry` at 0x2000000 that runs
    `blx 0x2000040` and `bl 0x2000080`, a Thumb `thumb_helper` symbol at
    0x2000041 (`movs r0,#7; bx lr`) and an A32 `arm_helper` symbol at
    0x2000080 (`add r0,r0,#1; bx lr`).

    Pass 1 (`armfuncmode off`, GH-842's image, no mapping symbols) reproduces
    the defect: the Thumb mode of `thumb_helper` (its symbol, and the `blx`)
    reaches `arm_helper`, which decodes as Thumb and runs off the image.
    Pass 2 (default) sets A32 at the even `arm_helper` symbol: `return a0 + 1`.

    Passes 3 and 4 use the image whose `blx` is a `nop`, so only the odd
    `thumb_helper` symbol carries Thumb: off is still wrong, default is right.

    Passes 5 and 6 use GH-842's image with `$a`/`$t`/`$a` mapping symbols. The
    pass paints nothing there, and both decode `arm_helper` as A32.

    The A32 paint covers a function symbol's size, cut at the next function
    symbol, and the Thumb mode resumes past it. A size-0 symbol states no
    extent and is skipped: pass 7 uses the image whose `arm_helper` has size
    0, and it still decodes as Thumb.

    Passes 8 and 9 use `arm_static_thumb_so_o2_le32`, a gcc -O2 armel shared
    object (`.dynsym` only) whose A32 `arm_export` follows the Thumb
    `thumb_first`: off it decodes as Thumb, by default it is the A32 loop
    `s += i ^ 0x33`.

    Pass 10 uses `arm_funcmode_helper_o2_le32.so` (clang -O2, linked with
    lld, stripped): the A32 export `a_func` calls an unsymbolized A32 static
    helper at 0x1020c with `bl`. The A32 extent grows over a direct A32
    branch target before the next function symbol, so the helper is not
    handed back to Thumb where the extent ends.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
